From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Monutchee <engineering@monutchee.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 23:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] boot.cmd.kria: use PARTUUID root for USB boot

The starter-kit Kria QEMU model exposes the WIC root disk as USB mass storage.
The default boot script passes root=LABEL=root, but the kernel's early root
mount path does not resolve LABEL= and disables rootwait as an invalid root.

When U-Boot loaded the boot script from USB, append a kernel-native root=
argument after the default command line. The later root= wins, while other
kernel arguments from KERNEL_COMMAND_APPEND remain intact.

Signed-off-by: Monutchee <engineering@monutchee.com>
---
 boot.cmd.kria | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/boot.cmd.kria b/boot.cmd.kria
index 51b7a88..3a91c6f 100644
--- a/boot.cmd.kria
+++ b/boot.cmd.kria
@@ -14,6 +14,14 @@ zynqmp pmufw node close
 
 # Starter Kit default boot args
 setenv bootargs 'earlycon console=ttyPS1,115200 init_fatal_sh=1 @@KERNEL_COMMAND_APPEND@@';
+if test "${devtype}" = "usb"; then
+        part uuid ${devtype} ${devnum}:@@PARTNUM@@ root_uuid;
+        if test -n "${root_uuid}"; then
+                setenv bootargs "${bootargs} root=PARTUUID=${root_uuid} ro rootwait";
+        else
+                setenv bootargs "${bootargs} root=/dev/sda@@PARTNUM@@ ro rootwait";
+        fi
+fi
 
 for boot_target in ${boot_targets};
 do
-- 
2.43.0
